//! Rust port of the cine-rec-engine INGEST lane (waves C+D). The
//! Python package stays the source of truth (rust-port plan); every
//! ported piece is proven against fixtures generated by running the
//! REAL Python modules.
//!
//! * [`rate`] — `ingest/rate.py`: the pure [`rate::TokenBucket`]
//!   policy (bit-exact golden trace from the real `RateLimiter` with
//!   a monkeypatched clock/sleep) plus the async
//!   [`rate::RateLimiter`] wrapper whose lock is held across the
//!   sleep, like `asyncio.Lock` in the original.
//! * [`exports`] — `ingest/exports.py` pure core: URL builders
//!   (byte-compatible), the strict [`exports::parse_export`], the
//!   lenient [`exports::parse_line`], the streaming
//!   [`exports::LineBuffer`] with its faithful
//!   unterminated-tail-is-dropped quirk, and the
//!   [`exports::entry_passes`] starter filters.
//! * [`loader`] — `ingest/loader.py` (wave D): row builders, catalog
//!   upserts and bridge MIRRORING through **the single table
//!   registry** (`cine_rec_db::SchemaMap` — every statement resolves
//!   `{t_*}` there, matching the Python loader's `tables.py` seam);
//!   live parity pins the resulting table states against the real
//!   Python loader on the same database. The HTTP half is the
//!   [`loader::TitleFetcher`] seam until wave E.
//! * [`cli`] — the argument surface of `ingest/cli.py` (bodies are
//!   wave E).
//! * [`pyval`] — Python conversion semantics over JSON (`int()`,
//!   `float()`, truthiness, `repr`); [`date`] — the slice of
//!   `datetime.date` the URL builders need.
//!
//! The wave-C private table registry was REMOVED when
//! `cine_rec_db::SchemaMap` landed: one registry, owned by the db
//! crate. `tests/schema_map_bridge.rs` still cross-checks SchemaMap
//! against the Python-generated `tables_cases.json` fixture
//! (decisions, active maps and rendered SQL; error MESSAGE texts are
//! SchemaMap's domain — see the queue note about the divergence).
//!
//! Wave E TODOs: HTTP fetcher + retry + pacing (`loader::TitleFetcher`
//! impl), `iter_export_ids` streaming, `latest_export_url` clock,
//! bootstrap/refresh orchestration, CLI bodies, pyo3 exposure.

pub mod cli;
pub mod date;
pub mod exports;
pub mod loader;
pub mod pyval;
pub mod rate;
